<%--<p><b>Our Residential Spring, Summer and Autumn Schools</b></p>
<p>Our residential schools are based on the principle of bringing practising British lawyers to train the lawyer/participants. These schools run both in the UK, in association with our sister company, Cambridge Legal English Centre, CLEC, and also in other countries outside the EU. </p>
<p>The courses cover a range of different professional development topics but are mostly focussed on preparation for the Cambridge University International Legal English Certificate (ILEC) exam. You can read more about the exam and the dates and venues of the ILEC preparation courses at our sister company’s website at www.clec.co.uk </p>
<p>There are many lawyers who cannot, for a variety of reasons, attend courses in the U K. By flying our trainers to the participant’s countries there is no need for our students to worry about visas, flights, long periods away from the office, etc.</p>
<p>There are a number of seminars and courses at each residential school. These can be as short as one day, or can last up to 2 weeks, depending upon what is requested in the marketing survey which we carry out in each region before we hold the residential schools. The results give us a very clear picture of what topics are of interest, the depth of knowledge requested, the numbers of attendees and the amount of time they have to study. This allows us to tailor courses to the participant’s requirements, rather than making participants fit in with our schedule and course content.</p>
<p>We arrange a variety of excursions for the participants and their families so that partners and children do not feel neglected.</p>
<p><b>For more information please contact us via email or phone +91 93932-66688</b></p>--%>

